nodecode-phone-harness is a rewrite of phone-harness's phone-harness/phone-harness:

  https://github.com/phone-harness/phone-harness
  commit 549d300e317a76ec8f493600cb04c69ba4f9d97d
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 shawn pana (LICENSE)

The rewrite keeps what the plugin gave a user: one tool the model calls with a
Python script, the helpers of the phone-harness package pre-imported for it, one
script at a time on the phone, a bound that kills the script and everything it
started, and a result that is what the script printed plus how it ended - the
same two output caps, the same 5 to 1800 second bound, the same
*_API_KEY / *_TOKEN / *_SECRET scrub of the child's environment, and the same
rule for which image path in the output counts as the screenshot. The Python
package is not rewritten and not bundled: the cell runs the copy the operator
installed, as the plugin ran the copy its host installed. Left out: the
plugin's classifier, which could skip the approval question for a script a
heuristic judged phone-only (bypassable, and the question is the point); the
attachment of the screenshot to the tool result, which needs host vision
internals - the path is named in the result and shown with the look verb; the
registration of the package's SKILL.md as an agent skill, whose helper list the
cell's help topic and description carry instead; and Hermes's own surfaces -
plugin data folders, approval rule keys, toolset selection - which Nodecode
does not have.
